  "abstract": "Test a minimal per-horizon calibration head: add a learned 32-dim bias vector to the base outputs, scaled by a small factor and regularized with L2 and zero-mean penalties. Hypothesis: dataset-wide per-horizon offset contributes to error on ScalarRamp. Keep MAE+curvature (\u03bb=1e\u22124), Adam lr=9e\u22124, clip=1.0, drop=0.05, p=36, H=128, learn_gamma=False.",
